            "title": "Inconsistent isTargetable usage as property or function",
            "severity": "medium",
            "file": "lib/core/PackageRepository.js",
            "line": 66,
            "explanation": "The code uses resolver.constructor.isTargetable as if it's a property in fetch method but calls resolver.constructor.isTargetable() as a function in _resolve method. This inconsistency may cause runtime errors if isTargetable is a function. Resolver.js defines isTargetable as a static function, so the fetch method usage without parentheses is incorrect.",
            "suggestion": "In PackageRepository.prototype.fetch(), change 'isTargetable = resolver.constructor.isTargetable;' to 'isTargetable = resolver.constructor.isTargetable();' to call the function as intended.",
